+`scripts/protect-artifacts.sh` separately on that attempt's directory beneath
+`logs/` and `result/`. It makes regular files read-only and directories
+readable/traversable but non-writable. It refuses paths outside those two trees
+and refuses trees containing symbolic links.
+
